---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
** Steps that are to be followed for building NEMO3D application on the AIX platform **
                             Written by Hoon Ryu.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The instruction should be followed step by step.
For those who have account in lear or hamlet, I recommand you do step 1~5 in lear or hamlet.

1. Get the latest version of the code from the repository.

2. Modify the make.inc file and select one of the builds for the AIX platform.

3. Execute the script patches_AIX_perform.

4. In ARPACK directory there is a file called ARmake.inc which need a minor 
   modification of the archive option. If you want a 32-bit compilation, make 
   ARFLAGS = -X 32 rv and -X 64 rv for 64-bit compilation.

5. If you do not have makeC++SharedLib_r command in your path then add it
to your path. It will most likely be available in /usr/vacpp/bin.

6. Now connect to cloud.cc.purdue.edu using ssh command. 
   The username and passwd will be same as those of your carrier account.

7. The compilation should be done in NanoRegatta, which you can access using 
   pbs interactive job. Since the compilation typically takes 2 hours, use 
   qsub command to access NanoRegatta :
 
   qsub -I -q nano -l nodes=1:ppn=1,walltime=2:00:00
   (you need an authorized account for 'nano' cue here.)

8. set XERCESCROOT to (your NEMO3D directory)/xerces-c-src2_1_0.

9. set OBJECT_MODE to 32 or 64, according to your preference of compilation.

10. To start the build process issue the gmake command.

These are the set of instructions that you need to follow for getting started quickly. 
Once the build process is complete the executable is created in the nemo3d/bin directory. 
There are sample input decks to run in the nemo3d/example directory, which can be used to test run the code.
The user has to specify on the command line the input deck for the nemo3d application to run.


